e is nothing  comparable to one who is awakened  it is in the nature of things that Joy  arises in a person free from remorse  Purity and impurity depend on oneself no  one can purify another  [Music]  ceasing to do evil cultivating the good  purifying the heart this is the teaching  of the Buddhas  understanding is the hardwood of  well-spoken words  [Music]  just as a solid rock is not shaken by  the storm even so the wise are not  affected by Praise or blame  [Music]  we will develop love we will practice it  we will make it both a way and a basis  there is no fear for one whose mind is  not filled with desire  [Music]  whatever is not yours let go of it  you're letting go of it will be for your  long-term happiness and benefit  [Music]  meditate do not delay lest you later  regret it  [Music]  whatever can arise can cease  [Music]

